Explanation of the fix:

- We added a `uniform float u_opacity;` declaration to the fragment shader.
- We then multiply the final `gl_FragColor` by `u_opacity`.
- The WebGL post–processing machinery will set `u_opacity` to the layer’s configured opacity value, restoring the expected behavior when you do `new Heatmap({ opacity: 0.1, … })`.
